From 406219c3f4b800b9010066a617b219b9fc34f5d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:41:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] vulkan: mul_mat_vec up to 16 columns on RDNA3/4 (MMVQ
 types), 9 for the float dequant kernels

Above 8 columns MUL_MAT took the matrix-matrix path (cm1 int8 MMQ / coopmat), which on gfx1151 runs at ~65-80
GB/s for 9..16 columns vs 150+ for the 8-column mat-vec. mul_mat_vec_max_cols is now 16; the per-type rule
(ggml_vk_mmv_max_cols) keeps 8 off RDNA3/4, uses up to 16 columns where the MMVQ (q8_1) kernel runs and 9 for
the float dequant kernels (q6_K, iq2/iq3), which fall behind MMQ above that. GGML_VK_MMV_MAX_COLS overrides.
Cold weights, us at n = 9/12/16: iq4_xs 17408x5120 716/718/723 -> 324/399/500, q5_K 762/757/772 -> 410/500/618,
q8_0 5120x6144 232/238/243 -> 195/211/234, q6_K 5120x17408 n=9 892 -> 709, iq3_s n=9 801 -> 587.
Verify-shape MUL_MAT cases extended to n=16 and the UD-IQ4_XS type mix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
